Renderer adjustments for the Switch's Mesa (nouveau) GL 4.3 stack (__SWITCH__).

- XF block words read as a whole uvec4 plus a component select, and the copy
  encoder's divisions by run-time values done in floats with an exact
  correction: same results, without the code Switch emulators (Eden) misread
  or cannot run (gx_shader.cpp, gx_render.cpp)
- matrix rows (R4) and normal rows (R3) read as whole uvec4 loads: the same
  values, and half the GLSL link time per program on the console's Mesa
- the window is the whole display from the start: the Switch's SDL sizes the
  framebuffer once, at creation (gx_platform.cpp)
- both sticks pressed together (L3 + R3) toggle the debug overlay, as the
  backtick key does on a PC (gx_platform.cpp)

